{
  "case_id": "2003-02-1371",
  "document_hash": "303372bb99f1d08ecc67139b5772a8b9f612b46fb86d786aee8c9c8c2e299fcb",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "303372bb99f1d08ecc67139b5772a8b9f612b46fb86d786aee8c9c8c2e299fcb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-303372bb99f1-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES:\nKAREN K. MITCHELL, ESQ., Chief Deputy Attorney General, Jefferson City, Missouri; on behalf of the Petitioner.\nIRVING L. GORNSTEIN, ESQ., Assistant to the Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the United States, as amicus curiae, supporting the Petitioner.\nAMY M. BARTHOLOW, ESQ., Assistant Public Defender, Columbia, Missouri; on behalf of the Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "303372bb99f1d08ecc67139b5772a8b9f612b46fb86d786aee8c9c8c2e299fcb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-303372bb99f1-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: May I just interrupt? You say the second warning removes the presumption as to the earlier unwarned statement. Why?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Irving L. Gornstein",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "303372bb99f1d08ecc67139b5772a8b9f612b46fb86d786aee8c9c8c2e299fcb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-303372bb99f1-0000-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GORNSTEIN: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court:\nAn officer's failure to give Miranda warnings before taking an initial statement does not presumptively taint the admissibility of a subsequent statement that has been preceded by Miranda warnings and an express waiver of Miranda rights. And the reason is that the risk of"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "303372bb99f1d08ecc67139b5772a8b9f612b46fb86d786aee8c9c8c2e299fcb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-303372bb99f1-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Because?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Amy M. Barthlow",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "303372bb99f1d08ecc67139b5772a8b9f612b46fb86d786aee8c9c8c2e299fcb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-303372bb99f1-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. BARTHOLOW: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: I'd like to get directly to what Justice Souter just mentioned, that when there's a systematic interrogation, things are different."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Amy M. Barthlow",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "303372bb99f1d08ecc67139b5772a8b9f612b46fb86d786aee8c9c8c2e299fcb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-303372bb99f1-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. BARTHOLOW: When police officers deliberately elicit incriminating statements from a suspect, then --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Amy M. Barthlow",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "303372bb99f1d08ecc67139b5772a8b9f612b46fb86d786aee8c9c8c2e299fcb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-303372bb99f1-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. BARTHOLOW: All of those. I think you're concerned about the risk of coercion."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Amy M. Barthlow",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "303372bb99f1d08ecc67139b5772a8b9f612b46fb86d786aee8c9c8c2e299fcb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-303372bb99f1-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. BARTHOLOW: Well, it undermines the free will. It's -- it -- the tactic is used to prevent the exercise of free will."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice (unspecified)",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "303372bb99f1d08ecc67139b5772a8b9f612b46fb86d786aee8c9c8c2e299fcb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-303372bb99f1-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Well then, why have we allowed admission of so many statements, you know, impeachment, public -- public interest, that sort of thing, that result from a situation where there weren't Miranda warnings given if -- if simply station house interrogation always produces coercion?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Bartholow",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "303372bb99f1d08ecc67139b5772a8b9f612b46fb86d786aee8c9c8c2e299fcb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-303372bb99f1-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. BARTHOLOW: I believe that sometimes the second statement may be admitted, and that's what Elstad said. Even in the presence of actual coercion, they said that it could be dispelled."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice (unspecified)",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "303372bb99f1d08ecc67139b5772a8b9f612b46fb86d786aee8c9c8c2e299fcb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-303372bb99f1-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Why does the intentionality or not of the failure to give the Miranda warning have anything to do with whether the second confession is voluntary or not?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1371",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "303372bb99f1d08ecc67139b5772a8b9f612b46fb86d786aee8c9c8c2e299fcb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-303372bb99f1-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The question is, does it render the first statement involuntary and therefore capable of tainting the second statement?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Mitchell",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1371",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "303372bb99f1d08ecc67139b5772a8b9f612b46fb86d786aee8c9c8c2e299fcb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-303372bb99f1-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Finally, what we are asking this Court to do is to reverse the Missouri court decision that focused on intent, deterrence, and the carrying forward of the presumption to taint the subsequent statement because each of those findings are inconsistent with this Court's holding in Elstad, and instead to apply the framework of Elstad to this case and to reverse."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1371",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "303372bb99f1d08ecc67139b5772a8b9f612b46fb86d786aee8c9c8c2e299fcb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-303372bb99f1-0003-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If there are no further questions."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
